msgstr ""

#: inc/form.php:159
msgid "Code from the front desk"
msgstr ""

#: inc/form.php:167
msgid "Send my hours"
msgstr ""

#: inc/form.php:171
msgid "Hours you send here are checked by staff before they count toward anything. Nothing you enter appears publicly."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:49
msgid "Setting up"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:50
msgid "Do these three things once, before anybody relies on a letter. Each takes a minute, and the letter is wrong in a way nobody notices until a court reads it if you skip the first."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:53
msgid "Set what appears on your letters"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:55
#: inc/help-content.php:66
#: inc/help-content.php:77
msgid "Go to <strong>Volunteer Tracker</strong> &rsaquo; <strong>Settings</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:56
msgid "Select the <strong>Letter</strong> tab."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:57
msgid "Enter your organization’s name, address, and the phone number or email address a court or school should use to check a letter."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:58
msgid "Enter the name and title of the person who signs."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:59
#: inc/help-content.php:70
#: inc/help-content.php:81
#: inc/help-content.php:381
msgid "Select <strong>Save Changes</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:61
msgid "Each of these falls back to something reasonable on its own — your site title, your administrator’s email address, an unlabeled line. Together those fallbacks produce a letter headed with a website’s title over a webmaster’s address."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:64
msgid "Choose who can verify hours and who can issue letters"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:67
msgid "Select the <strong>Permissions</strong> tab."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:68
msgid "Select the roles that may mark hours verified."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:69
msgid "Select the roles that may produce letters."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:72
msgid "These are separate on purpose. The coordinator who knows the work happened and the director who signs a letter to a probation officer are often different people."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:75
msgid "Decide how long to keep records"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:78
msgid "Select the <strong>Privacy</strong> tab."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:79
msgid "Choose how long a volunteer’s record is kept after their last activity."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:80
msgid "Choose whether records are anonymized or deleted when that time passes."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:83
msgid "Anonymizing keeps the hours and removes the name, which is usually what an organization wants: the service record still counts toward your reporting and identifies nobody."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:91
msgid "Hours reach a letter only after somebody on your staff says the work happened. That is two steps, and they are deliberately separate."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:96
#: inc/help-content.php:330
msgid "Go to <strong>Volunteer Tracker</strong> &rsaquo; <strong>Volunteers</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:97
msgid "Select <strong>Add New Volunteer</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:98
msgid "Enter their name, and their email address if you have one."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:99
msgid "If a court or school required a number of hours, enter how many, by when, and who required them."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:100
#: inc/help-content.php:111
msgid "Select <strong>Publish</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:102
msgid "A volunteer is not a WordPress user. No account is created, no password is set, and they never log in."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:107
#: inc/help-content.php:118
#: inc/help-content.php:128
msgid "Go to <strong>Volunteer Tracker</strong> &rsaquo; <strong>Hours</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:108
msgid "Select <strong>Log one shift</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:109
msgid "Start typing the volunteer’s name and select them from the list."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:110
msgid "Enter the date, how long they worked, and what they did."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:113
msgid "Enter the duration however you say it: 3.5, 3:30, 3h 30m, or 210m all work. The figure stored is rounded to the increment you chose in Settings — always to the nearest, never up — and the screen tells you when it has rounded."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:116
msgid "Log a whole day from a sign-in sheet"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:119
msgid "Select <strong>Log a day</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:120
msgid "Enter the date, the times, and what the work was. These are used for every row."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:121
msgid "Add a row for each person on the sheet."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:122
#: inc/help-content.php:232
msgid "Select <strong>Log these hours</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:129
msgid "Select <strong>Waiting to verify</strong>, above the list."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:130
msgid "Read the shifts waiting, which are grouped by the person they are about."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:131
msgid "Select <strong>Verify</strong> beside each one you can confirm happened."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:133
msgid "Your name and the date are recorded, and both appear on any letter that includes those hours. Only verified hours reach a letter."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:136
msgid "Match hours somebody sent in themselves"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:138
msgid "Go to <strong>Volunteer Tracker</strong> &rsaquo; <strong>Hours</strong>, then <strong>Waiting to verify</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:139
msgid "Select <strong>Match them now</strong> in the notice at the top."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:140
msgid "Open the entry and select <strong>Attach to</strong> the right person."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:141
msgid "If they are not on file yet, select <strong>Create a volunteer from this</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:142
msgid "Verify the hours as usual."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:144
msgid "Anything sent through the public form arrives attached to nobody. What somebody typed is a claim until a person says whose it is."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:152
msgid "A letter reports what your organization recorded. You write it on the volunteer’s own record: start a draft, issue it when you are happy with it, then send it. It carries a reference code so anybody who receives it can phone you and check it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:155
msgid "Draft a letter"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:157
#: inc/help-content.php:339
msgid "Go to <strong>Volunteer Tracker</strong> &rsaquo; <strong>Volunteers</strong> and open the person’s record."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:158
msgid "Find <strong>Verification letters</strong> and select <strong>Draft a verification letter</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:159
msgid "Choose <strong>Everything on record</strong>, or <strong>A period</strong> if a court or a school asked about particular months."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:160
msgid "If it is going to somebody other than the volunteer, fill in who it is addressed to and what it is about."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:161
msgid "Select <strong>Save the draft</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:163
msgid "A draft is fixed at the moment you make it. It states what you had verified that day, and shifts verified afterwards will not join it — so if hours are still waiting, verify them first and start the draft after. Nothing is sent and nothing is logged until you issue it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:166
msgid "Issue it and send it"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:168
msgid "Select <strong>Open</strong> on the draft to read the letter it would produce. Reading one records nothing."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:169
msgid "Select <strong>Issue it</strong>. The letter gets its reference code and goes into your log. It has not been sent to anybody yet."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:170
msgid "Then select <strong>Print</strong>, <strong>Post</strong> or <strong>Email</strong> on the issued row."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:172
msgid "Each of the three is recorded against the letter with the date, and Post and Email also record who it went to — so the log answers “did you send it to us”, not only “a letter was produced”. Email offers the address on the record or one you type. To save a PDF, choose Print and then your browser’s Save as PDF; the plugin does not bundle a PDF library."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:175
msgid "Check a reference code somebody phoned about"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:177
msgid "Go to <strong>Volunteer Tracker</strong> &rsaquo; <strong>Dashboard</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:178
msgid "Find the <strong>Check a reference</strong> panel."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:179
msgid "Enter the code the caller reads to you."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:180
msgid "Select <strong>Check it</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:182
msgid "You are told whether the code matches a letter you issued and whether it still says what your records say. A shift verified since the letter went out does not disturb the answer — the letter is checked against what you had attested to on the day it was fixed. You are not told anything the caller is not already holding."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:190
msgid "A scheduled shift is a plan. Nobody accrues hours by signing up — turning a finished shift into hours is something a person does afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:193
msgid "Schedule a shift"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:195
#: inc/help-content.php:247
msgid "Go to <strong>Volunteer Tracker</strong> &rsaquo; <strong>Schedule</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:196
msgid "Select <strong>Add</strong>, then <strong>Add New Shift</strong> — the other choice is for an occasion with several roles on it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:197
msgid "Enter the date, the start and end times, and what the work is."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:198
msgid "Enter how many people you need and how many you have room for."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:199
msgid "To repeat it, choose a pattern and a date to repeat until."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:200
msgid "Select <strong>Add to the schedule</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:202
msgid "Every occurrence of a repeat is a real shift you can edit or call off on its own."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:205
msgid "Change every occurrence of a repeat"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:207
msgid "Open any occurrence from the schedule."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:208
msgid "Select <strong>Change the whole repeat</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:209
msgid "Select each thing you want to change, and enter the new value."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:210
msgid "Read how many occurrences will change and how many will be left."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:211
msgid "Select <strong>Change these occurrences</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:213
msgid "Occurrences that have already happened, and ones you called off, are left alone unless you say otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:216
msgid "Put somebody on a shift"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:218
#: inc/help-content.php:350
msgid "Open the shift from the schedule."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:219
msgid "Find <strong>Who is coming</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:220
msgid "Start typing a name and select the volunteer."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:221
msgid "Select <strong>Add them</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:223
msgid "If the shift is full, the person goes on a waiting list and moves up automatically when somebody withdraws."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:226
msgid "Turn a finished shift into hours"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:228
msgid "Open the shift after it has happened."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:229
msgid "Select <strong>Log the hours</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:230
msgid "Clear the checkbox beside anybody who did not turn up."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:231
msgid "Add a row for anybody who came without signing up."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:234
msgid "Everybody who signed up is already selected, with the scheduled times filled in. The hours still have to be verified, like any others."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:241
msgid "Running an event"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:242
msgid "An event is one occasion with several roles on it — a festival, a meal service, a collection drive. A shift is one job, which may come round again. Everything under an event is an ordinary shift, so rosters, reminders, waiting lists and hours behave exactly as they do for a shift you scheduled on its own."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:245
msgid "Set up an event"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:248
msgid "Select <strong>Add</strong>, then <strong>Add New Event</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:249
msgid "Enter the name volunteers will recognize it by, and where it is."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:250
msgid "Name the first role — greeters, kitchen, clean-up — and enter its times, with how many people each one needs and has room for."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:251
msgid "Select <strong>+ Add another time</strong> for each further time in that role, and <strong>+ Add another role</strong> for the next role."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:252
msgid "Select <strong>Create the event</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:254
msgid "There is no date field on the event itself. The dates come from the times in the grid, so an event that spans two days needs no telling. A supervisor, address or note typed on the event carries down to every role that does not name its own."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:257
msgid "Put an event where volunteers can see it"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:259
msgid "Publish the event, and switch signing up on under <strong>Volunteer Tracker</strong> &rsaquo; <strong>Settings</strong> if it is not on already."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:260
msgid "Edit the page or post you want the event to appear on."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:261
msgid "Add the <strong>Volunteer Event</strong> block and choose this event."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:262
msgid "Update the page and read it as a visitor would."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:264
msgid "Publishing an event does not give it a web address. It is seen only where you place it, which is why a page has to be chosen. Volunteers see the roles, the times and how many places are left — never who else signed up."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:267
msgid "Put somebody on one of an event’s times"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:269
msgid "Open the event’s <strong>Roster</strong> from the schedule."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:270
msgid "Find the role and the time you are filling."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:271
msgid "Under <strong>Put somebody on</strong>, start typing a name and select the volunteer."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:272
msgid "Select <strong>Give them a place</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:274
msgid "The roster flags anybody down for two times that overlap, and anybody short of a credential the role asks for. Neither stops you — they are things to know before the day, not refusals."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:277
msgid "Turn an event into hours"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:279
msgid "Open the event’s <strong>Roster</strong> after the day."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:280
msgid "Select <strong>Log the hours</strong> beside the first time that has finished."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:281
msgid "Clear the checkbox beside anybody who did not turn up, and add a row for anybody who came without signing up."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:282
msgid "Select <strong>Log these hours</strong>, and repeat for each remaining time."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:284
msgid "One time at a time, because a festival’s kitchen and its clean-up crew worked different hours. The event’s row says how many of its times still need writing up, and the hours still have to be verified, like any others."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:287
msgid "Run the same event again"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:289
msgid "Open the event and find <strong>Other things you can do</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:290
msgid "Under <strong>Run it again on</strong>, enter the date it happens next."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:291
msgid "For a series, choose a rhythm and a date to stop. Leave the rhythm as you found it for a single copy."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:292
msgid "Select <strong>Copy this event</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:293
msgid "Open each copy, check the dates, and publish it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:295
msgid "Copies carry the roles, the times, the numbers and the credentials each one asks for, and nobody who signed up. They arrive as drafts, so nothing is public until you have read it. Each run is a whole event of its own — calling off October leaves November alone."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:302
msgid "Tracking credentials"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:303
msgid "A credential is something a volunteer has to hold — a training course, a signed waiver, a background check. It is not the same as hours a court required, which live on the volunteer’s own record."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:306
msgid "Define a credential"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:308
#: inc/help-content.php:320
#: inc/help-content.php:360
msgid "Go to <strong>Volunteer Tracker</strong> &rsaquo; <strong>Credentials</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:309
msgid "Select <strong>Add New Credential</strong>, beside the heading."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:310
msgid "Enter what it is called, as you would say it out loud."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:311
msgid "Enter how many months it lasts, or 0 if it never expires."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:312
msgid "Choose what happens when somebody has not got it: report it, or stop them signing up."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:313
msgid "Select <strong>Add it</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:315
msgid "Reporting is the safer choice and what most organizations want. Stopping a signup is for the things nobody may work without."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:318
msgid "Change a credential you already defined"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:321
msgid "Hover the one you want and select <strong>Edit</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:322
msgid "Change the name, the renewal interval, what happens when somebody has not got it, or the note."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:323
msgid "Select <strong>Save this credential</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:325
msgid "Renaming is safe — every record points at the credential itself. Changing the interval is not the same kind of change: expiry is worked out from it every time it is asked for, so a shorter interval can make somebody lapsed the moment you save. The form says how many people hold it before you change that field."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:328
msgid "Mark somebody inactive who has stopped volunteering"
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:331
msgid "Hover the row for the person who has stopped."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:332
msgid "Select <strong>Make inactive</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: inc/help-content.php:334
msgid "It keeps everything: their hours, their name, and their name on any letter already issued. It stops them being offered when you are staffing a shift, and takes them off the overdue list. Select <strong>Inactive</strong> above the list to see them, and <strong>Make active</strong> on the row to undo it. This is not anonymizing and not deleting — those are on the volunteer’s own record and answer a privacy question instead."
msgstr ""

